 "brief": "A SURVEY OF TWISTED ALEXANDER POLYNOMIALS — We give a short introduction to the theory of twisted Alexander polynomials of a 3–manifold associated to a representation of its fundamental group.",
 "extended": "**A SURVEY OF TWISTED ALEXANDER POLYNOMIALS**\n\n*STEFAN FRIEDL AND STEFANO VIDUSSI*\n\n42 pp, 48 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** We give a short introduction to the theory of twisted Alexander polynomials of a 3–manifold associated to a representation of its fundamental group. We summarize their formal properties and we explain their relationship to twisted Reidemeister torsion. We then give a survey of the many applications of twisted invariants to the study of topological problems. We conclude with a short summary of the theory of higher order Alexander polynomials.\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; 1 Introduction; 2 Definition and basic properties; 2.1 Twisted Reidemeister torsion; 2.2 Computation of twisted Reidemeister torsio; 2.3 Torsion invariants; 2.4 Twisted Alexander invariants; 2.5 Computation of twisted Alexander polynomia; 3 Basic properties of twisted invariants; 3.1 Relationship between twisted invariants; 3.2 Twisted invariants for conjugate represent; 3.3 Change of variables; 3.4 Duality for twisted invariants; 3.5 Shapiro's lemma for twisted invariants; 3.6 Twisted invariants of knots and links; 4 Distinguishing knots and links; 5 Twisted Alexander polynomials and concordanc; 5.1 Twisted Alexander polynomials of zero–surg",
